From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:26:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: parser: Clear each mode before parsing it

The mode array comes from kmalloc_array(), and a rejected mode leaves
its slot to the next one. parse_mode() sets the VRR fields and the score
only when the firmware provides them, so a mode could inherit them from
heap contents or from the rejected mode.

Signed-off-by: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
[Youwes09: from Gravity Linux a8aa5e2f7d1d]
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/parser.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/parser.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/parser.c
index d0b20f2d2035..b546a426733c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/parser.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/parser.c
@@ -605,6 +605,10 @@ struct dcp_display_mode *enumerate_modes(struct dcp_parse_ctx *handle,
 
 	for (; it.idx < it.len; ++it.idx) {
 		mode = &modes[*count];
+		/* Optional fields (including VRR) must not inherit heap contents or
+		 * a rejected mode that reused this slot. */
+		memset(mode, 0, sizeof(*mode));
+		score = -1;
 		ret = parse_mode(it.handle, mode, &score, width_mm, height_mm, notch_height);
 
 		/* Errors for a single mode are recoverable -- just skip it. */
